  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 403 AM CDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nThe LREF continues to show an unseasonably strong upper high \nbuilding over southeastern CONUS setting up southwesterly flow \nacross Missouri and Illinois Tuesday into Thursday. This will \nbring 850mb temperatures of 20-22C Tuesday into Thursday (98th \npercentile) which supports the NBM having high temperatures in \nthe 90s over most of the area. With this said, there will be a \nstalled front in the area beneath the upper flow, quite possibly\nacross the northern CWA with the NBM 25th/75th percentile \nspread at UIN from Tuesday-Thursday being 8-12 degrees compared\nto STL which is only 3-4 degrees. This spread increases at STL \nlate in the week as the upper ridge weakens and the upper flow \nbecomes zonal which increases the chance the front moves south.\n\nWith highs in the 90s Tuesday into Thursday and dewpoints back in \nthe 70s, heat index readings of 100-105+ are forecast mainly along \nand south of I-70 Tuesday into Thursday.  The chance for dangerous \nheat is expected to drop off by end of the week as the front moves \nsouth bringing clouds and a chance of rain.\n\nThe LREF has 40-70% of it members producing rain at UIN Tuesday into \nWednesday with WPC highlighting the northern part of the CWA in a \nslight risk for excessive rainfall.  Can't rule out some locally \nheavy rainfall in this part of the CWA during this time frame.  The \nLREF also shows 30-50% of members producing rain at STL Thursday \ninto Saturday as the front potentially moves southward.",
